FSTAB(5)                    File Formats                     FSTAB(5)

NAME
    fstab - filesystems mounted at boot

SYNOPSIS
    /etc/fstab

DESCRIPTION
    Each line names a device, a mount point, a filesystem type and an
    optional comma separated list of options; # starts a comment. The
    device is a name under /dev, with or without the /dev/ prefix. The
    types are mfs and fat.

OPTIONS
    defaults   no option
    nofail     a device that cannot be mounted is skipped without error
    noauto     the entry is not mounted by fsinit
    seed=DIR   copy the tree below DIR into the mount point when the
               mounted filesystem is empty
    uid=N      owner of every file of a fat volume (default 0)
    gid=N      group of every file of a fat volume (default 0)
    umask=OOO  permission bits removed from the files of a fat volume
               (default 022), which keeps no permissions of its own

    The last three options are passed to the filesystem, and mfs accepts
    none, since it stores owners and permissions itself.

EXAMPLE
    vdc /home mfs nofail,seed=/usr/share/skel/home

SEE ALSO
    fsinit(1), mount(1)
